        "Farm and factory seasons matter too. The sugar crushing season runs roughly from late autumn into spring, stretching shifts for factory staff, and the kharif harvest in October pulls many farming households into the fields. The school breaks, above all the summer vacation and the gap around Diwali, remain the best windows for a focused block of lessons.",
        "On the examination side, Maharashtra's HSC and SSC papers come in February and March, and CBSE starts in February and runs into April. International candidates have more choice: Cambridge offers a May-June and an October-November series, Edexcel adds January, and the IB runs in May and November. A student enrolled at a school elsewhere keeps to that school's calendar, while a private IGCSE candidate can pick the series that fits their preparation.",
