  faqs: [
    { question: "Who teaches IB Mathematics to a student living in Majalgaon?", answer: "A tutor based in another Indian city, matched to the course your child follows. Nobody in Manjlegaon has taught the IB syllabus, so the search is national: you send the course, level and exam date, we propose a tutor who has taught that paper, and the student meets them live on screen for a free first lesson." },
    { question: "Can a tutor come to our house in Manjlegaon for IGCSE lessons?", answer: "No. Nobody from IB Gram comes to the house in Manjlegaon, because in-person home tuition is run in Gurugram and a few parts of Delhi NCR and nowhere else. What your child gets instead is one-to-one private tuition at home on a laptop, with the tutor on screen and a shared whiteboard. For IB and IGCSE work the learning is very much the same." },
    { question: "Which IGCSE board should a private candidate from Beed district choose?", answer: "Either Cambridge or Pearson Edexcel can work; universities accept both. Decide on exam dates, on which centre will take a private entry, and on which specification the tutor has taught most recently. Tell us the subjects and we compare the two syllabuses for your child, including where the wording and mark schemes differ." },
    { question: "What makes one tutor's fee different from another's?", answer: "Course level, how specialised the subject is, the tutor's experience with that exact syllabus and the hours you want each week. You get a figure in writing before you book. Because lessons are online, there is no travel element in it, and there is no fixed term, so a family can pause or stop whenever it needs to." },
    { question: "Do any schools around Manjlegaon teach the IB or IGCSE?", answer: "None that we could confirm. The directories we checked show State Board and CBSE schools in the town and across the district. Chhatrapati Sambhajinagar, Pune and Hyderabad are where families look for international schools, and some begin with online lessons while they weigh a move. If you know of a campus we have missed, tell us and we will check it." },
    { question: "Our family is returning from the Gulf. Will a tutor continue my child's current IB course?", answer: "Yes. Send the subject list, the latest reports and the exam session, and a tutor takes the course up at the same level, following the old school's order of topics for as long as you wish. That spares a child the gap between leaving one programme and finding another." },
    { question: "Is the first lesson really free?", answer: "Yes. It is a complete lesson on a real topic with the tutor proposed for your child, not a sales call. Only afterwards do you decide whether to continue, and the written plan for the first month is prepared after that decision, not before it." },
    { question: "What help is allowed with the IA and the Extended Essay?", answer: "A tutor can explain the criteria, sharpen a research question, check a method and respond to the student's own draft. Drafting or rewriting the assessed piece breaks IB integrity rules, so every request of that kind is declined. The same applies to TOK essays and IGCSE coursework." },
    { question: "Which Diploma subjects can we get a tutor for?", answer: "The usual spread: Maths AA and AI, Physics, Chemistry, Biology, Economics, Business Management, English A, Computer Science, Psychology, Geography, History and Environmental Systems, along with TOK and Extended Essay guidance. Hindi B tutors are available for the language course, and we can look for other subjects on request." },
    { question: "Can a Class 7 student on MYP or a Class 3 student on PYP be taught online?", answer: "Yes. MYP lessons cover writing to criteria, scientific reasoning and the Personal Project; PYP lessons cover reading, number sense and the research habits behind the Exhibition. Shorter, more frequent sessions often suit younger children, so a PYP timetable usually looks different from a Diploma one." },
    { question: "Will a screen lesson work as well as a tutor in the room?", answer: "For IB and IGCSE work the two come close, because what counts is explanation, worked examples and marked papers, and a shared screen carries all three. It also brings in specialists that no town of Manjlegaon's size could supply. Steady internet is the main requirement, and a tablet with a pen helps in Maths." },
    { question: "How do you decide whether a tutor is good enough?", answer: "We look at qualifications, how recently the tutor taught the same subject and level, and how they work with assessment criteria. In a town without a specialist pool, recent experience of the syllabus is the test that matters, and the trial lesson lets you verify it first hand before committing to anything." },
    { question: "When should a Manjlegaon student start IGCSE or IB lessons?", answer: "At the start of the course if possible: Grade 9 for IGCSE and Class 11 for the Diploma. Early lessons repair foundations before mocks and predicted grades start to count. A start in the final year still helps if it targets past papers and the topics carrying the most marks, though the gain is narrower." },
    { question: "Can a State Board student add IGCSE Maths without leaving school?", answer: "Yes. The main adjustment is in how questions are phrased and marked. Command words such as explain, evaluate and justify are taught directly, and written reasoning is practised from the first week. Starting one or two terms ahead of the chosen sitting keeps the load manageable next to school and homework." },
    { question: "Which hours are lessons held in summer?", answer: "Mostly weekday evenings after school and weekend mornings, and in April and May the slot moves later, after the worst of the afternoon heat. We steer clear of Ganeshotsav, Diwali and State Board exam weeks where we can. A second weekly slot is easy to add before an exam." },
    { question: "We have power cuts in summer. What then?", answer: "Tell us at the start and the plan is built around it. Typical fixes are a wired connection or a strong mobile signal, a phone hotspot as a spare, a small inverter for the router, lighter sessions in the hottest weeks and a recording of any class that drops." },
    { question: "What if the tutor is not the right fit?", answer: "Tell us and we will arrange someone else, without any awkwardness. Reviews happen every few weeks in any case, and because there is no contract, pausing or stopping costs the family nothing. A good match matters more than politeness to the first tutor." },
    { question: "Does IB Gram belong to any school or exam board?", answer: "No. IB Gram is an independent tutoring service with no connection to any Majalgaon or Beed school, to the IB organisation, to Cambridge or to Pearson Edexcel. Any school names on this page describe the setting and are not endorsements." },
  ],

